e here putting in that  time and sustained effort there's also a  lot of other interests and there's other  ways there's other ways we have agency  and power to deal with this money and to  deal with the money associated with  nuclear weapons raise your hand if you  have a bank account yeah  oh wow that's like everyone because just  about everybody does and we can use our  power as account holders to deal with  nuclear weapons and so I want to talk a  little bit about what it is that that I  do to help you to use your power as an  account holder so I create this report  don't bank on the bomb every year  and we look at a few key things we look  at the companies that are publicly  traded and are involved in nuclear  weapons programs so we look at last in  this last year's report 26 companies  here are their logos we put it all up on  our website and they're making the key  components now these are not guys that  are making screws you know these are not  guys I'm making toilets these are guys  that are making key components necessary  for nuclear weapons to be detonated okay  so these are twice it's companies we  update this list every year we do very  strict and I'm really a stickler for  detail very strict and a hard core  analysis and we verify and consult with  them to make sure their contracts are  current and when it comes to to nuclear  inspections sometimes we change the list  because a company will have ended its  contract and then we find out Oh company  changes its name Babcock &amp; Wilcox sold  off part of its division to bwx tech  oh geez so we change and update our  information we want to make this  information as accurate and as usable as  possible for you the bank account holder  because a lot of banks have policies on  where and how they will invest your  money banks have policies insurance  companies have policies pension funds  have policies we look at those policies  we put together we call the Hall of Fame  right now our Hall of Fame is primarily  in Europe so we need to get some more  Americans going you know on this Hall of  Fame thing these are companies our Hall  of Fame our companies that have the  ultimate gold standard of policy they  will not put any money into any company  that has anything to do with nuclear  weapons all right these are great and  they they make sure they invest they  won't invest in the whole company so a  company like Boeing also makes planes  Airbus also makes planes these financial  institutions are Hall of Fame won't  invest in those companies they won't say  oh we but that we invest in good  projects like like new airplanes no no  they say the whole company is excluded  and this is important this is one of our  criteria and then we talk to these  financial institutions we say you know  what is it that you need to have a good  policy because we have a Hall of Fame  but we also have a runners-up in between  2014 and 2015 we added 30 new financial  institutions to our runners-up category  30 new institutions that say oh we'll do  something to limit our investment in  nuclear weapon production so something  is better than nothing  something means that they heard from  their clients they heard from people who  say I don't want my money to touch  nuclear weapons and they're at least  doing something and then we work with  them we say yeah well you know you did  something but it's not good enough so  you're not a hall-of-famer yet how can  we get you there  and last week we got to pension funds  the Dutch railway pension funds you know  they're gonna go in the Hall of Fame  because they added another company to  their exclusion list they said oh you  saw your report we didn't believe that  this company Moog had anything to do  with nuclear weapons but then we did our  own investigation we found out yeah  you're right will divest from them  immediately and we said great now we'll  be able to make sure that you're on our  Hall of Fame and a Hall of Fame we check  to make sure they implement the policy  and then of course we have a Hall of  Shame because you know you got to point  out who has investment it's important  for us to know who are who are the  people who are making this money  available you know who is it's in who is  it that lets the companies get these  loans that lets that puts these  revolving credit facilities who has  assets with these companies owns their  shares their stocks their bonds 382  financial institutions do most of those  are actually here in the US but they're  not only there for a bunch of other  companies other countries as well it's  actually uh yeah 27 countries overall  that there that are financial  institutions that are Hall of Shame and  we publish this list we put their names  out there so people know is my bank  banking on the bomb or not and it's  important because if you don't have the  information you can't do anything right  it's kind of key and then we help and  provide support as much as we can for  campaigns campaigns are awesome doing  something feels good doing something  about nuclear weapons feels really good  to be able to do something about this  and you know what it doesn't take a lot  of people we got Swedbank in sweden to  divest because we got one person got to  a journalist who was freaked out by how  many banks in Sweden were involved in  nuclear weapons and connected to nuclear  weapons got a front-page story and also  know these people posted stuff on that  banks on  Red Bank Facebook page saying what you  can't put nuclear weapons you can't put  my money in nuclear weapons we can't we  can't be connected with this no no no no  it's not Swedish we've got you know and  so in that band that you know one person  then within said Bank changed the policy  now they're they're pretty good really  excited that campaigns going on in the  UK the Royal Bank of Scotland in Germany  and Belgium and Sweden as I said in  Austria in Australia and we're you know  things are picking up here really happy  that things are also picking up here we  also have a little tool on our website  now I'm not a big technical person so  maybe there's some great technical  people who couldn't help us make this  tool a little bit better but we have a  little thing you can send a message to  financial institutions through our  website directly so don't bank on the  bomb calm and you can click on the send  a message and then you can send these  financial institutions directly just you  know put in your name and say oh this is  my bank I want you to get your money out  of nuclear weapons you can click to  tweet at them we've uploaded their  Twitter addresses and stuff like that  I'm a big person on Twitter I'd love to  do it and there's always an excellent  tool that I think some of you I have  some of you may also have GF banking on  your phone like you can check your  balance and stuff like that there's a  little icon generally little mailbox you  can send a message to your bank and ask  them a question you can do that right  now  there's free Wi-Fi here you can do it  right now and you can say do you have a  policy on nuclear weapons is my money  connected to nuclear weapons I don't  want it to be when you take that tiny  little action you start a reaction and  it's not a kind of you know fissile act  for some you know chain reaction but  it's a good one yeah and it's something  that that everybody can do and I hope  and encourage everyone to do and if  you'd like to learn more please get in  touch with me tweet at me call me  send me an email and I'm happy to talk  to you all and thank you very much great  thank you Susie well we have time for  just a couple of questions for Jonathan  and Susie yes  now we cannot be that easy who says a  lot of doable work is no Constitution  but it's just  Susie you have state-by-state listings  of nuclear firms operating across the  country and in turn we don't have the  capacity to put that together  we do however work a lot of other people  kind of information well we can't put  that together ourselves tell you why ask  Walt Havenstein who lost from the  governorship in New Hampshire its mr.  BAE oh yeah yeah and in 2014 he was  running for governor at the same time  the Scott Brown was running for the for  the Senate so what you had was the  military-industrial complex running to  run the state of New Hampshire so any  data we can get from anybody by way of  state-by-state breakdown smite helped  thanks a lot okay thanks  time for one more one more question yes  when you talk about companies that are  making nuclear weapons are you also  including companies that are  manufacturing the delivery vehicles we  talk about the warheads themselves a lot  of companies do both but because of a  resource brilliance resource restraint  we are limited in what we can put out  there there is you know we've had some  it's important to look at that  but we only can do as much as man the  Internet can do I just want to say  quickly that as individuals or whoever  we are I think we really need to target  both I know your constraints but also  anybody who has something that they  believe is a socially responsible  investment look again because it's  shocking what some of those funds invest  in we see we have a need in the u.s. to  have research come together and target  the military-industrial complex and the  delivery systems okay well thank you

